@startuml
title KiwiDB — Deployment Diagram
skinparam shadowing false

node "Client Device" as Client {
  artifact "React SPA\n(browser)" as SPA
}

node "Host Machine (single server)" as Host {

  node "Python Runtime (main process)" as Main {
    component "uvicorn + FastAPI\n(REST + WebSocket)" as Web
    component "LSMEngine\n(asyncio event loop)" as Engine
    component "FlushPipeline" as FP
    component "CompactionManager" as CM
    artifact "TCP Log Broadcast\nserver :9009" as Log
  }

  node "Compaction Subprocess\n(ProcessPoolExecutor)" as Sub {
    component "run_compaction()\n(own interpreter + GIL)" as Worker
  }

  node "Local Disk (data_root)" as Disk {
    artifact "config.json" as Cfg
    artifact "WAL file" as Wal
    folder "sstable/L0..L3/<uuid7>/" as SSTDir {
      artifact "data.bin" as Data
      artifact "index.bin" as Index
      artifact "filter.bin" as Filter
      artifact "meta.json" as Meta
    }
  }
}

SPA --> Web : HTTP / WebSocket
Web --> Engine : in-process calls

Engine --> Wal : append / replay / truncate
Engine --> SSTDir : read (mmap) / write
Engine --> Cfg : load / save
FP --> SSTDir : write new L0 tables
CM --> Sub : submit task (pickled)\nvia asyncio.to_thread
Worker --> SSTDir : read inputs / write merged output
Engine ..> Log : emit structured logs
Log ..> Client : live log stream (TCP / WS)

note right of Sub
  Separate OS process = separate GIL.
  CPU-heavy merge runs on another core
  while the main process keeps serving.
end note

@enduml
